#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
scattershot3.py — Network Reconnaissance Tool

Performs host discovery, port scanning, web-service probing, banner
grabbing, SSL/TLS analysis, and Nuclei vulnerability scanning.
Accepts individual IPs, hyphen ranges (192.168.1.1-20), CIDR blocks,
inline target arguments, and a --targets-file containing one entry per line.

All targets are automatically classified as INTERNAL (RFC-1918 / private
address space) or EXTERNAL (publicly routable) and scanned in separate
passes.  Output is written to a two-level project directory:

    <project>/
    ├── internal/          ← RFC-1918 / private targets
    │   ├── nmap/
    │   ├── sslscan/
    │   ├── testssl/
    │   ├── nuclei/
    │   ├── banners/
    │   ├── scan.log
    │   ├── scan.log.json
    │   ├── errors.log
    │   ├── findings.json
    │   ├── findings.csv
    │   ├── software_inventory.json
    │   ├── web_ports.txt
    │   ├── web_targets.txt
    │   ├── correlated.json
    │   └── results.json
    ├── external/          ← publicly routable targets
    │   └── (same structure)
    └── summary.json       ← combined cross-scope summary

Works on Linux, macOS, and Windows.
"""
